 "text": "This book showed me my future. Ten years from now the car, the house, the life I only ever wrote about, from where I said it looked impossible. Then the book took me back to where it started, one page, a dream that looked unachievable, written down anyway. After that it was choices, small ones, every day. Go out or build, scroll or start, there was always a choice. His only job was to make it. Not every choice was right, his first company failed. He adjusted and chose again. Every scene, every choice. Each one pushed his life in a direction, some split apart, some came back together, all of it connected. And every line led to the same place. So I turned to the first page and wrote mine. That's what Demure is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do.",
